Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 12:20:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(memory): push memory to agents via SessionStart hook +
 wire auto-file rail
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Memory was 100% pull (orphaned): an agent only saw remembered notes if it typed
`forge recall`. And ensureBackingIssue() — the "nothing goes missing" primitive —
had zero callers. This makes memory PUSH and wires the auto-file rail.

FIX 1 — memory push (48d67c91):
- New context intent `memory-inject` (kind: 'context') in FORGE_HOOK_CONTRACT.
  Enforcement intents stay adapter-backed/fail-closed; context intents route to
  the `forge` CLI/fail-open. Claude renders a SessionStart hook; cursor/codex/
  hermes carry honest, tested capability-matrix skip reasons (never faked parity).
- `forge hooks session-start --harness <h>` emits harness-native SessionStart JSON
  (Claude additionalContext). Backed by lib/memory-digest.js: bounded (~400 tok via
  orientation.applyBudget) digest of top remembered notes + ready/claimed issues.
  Fail-open: empty/error -> no injection, never throws.
- buildOrientationSections gains a bounded MEMORY (remembered_notes) section so
  `forge prime`/orient surface remembered notes (opens+closes its own kernel driver).

FIX 2 — auto-file rail (a4b8f56f):
- Wire ensureBackingIssue into `forge worktree create`, `forge push`, and a new
  non-blocking lefthook pre-push (scripts/auto-backing-issue.js). Idempotent,
  best-effort, degrade+warn — never blocks the command.

Design: docs/work/2026-07-13-memory-push/design.md

Issues: 48d67c91-2ea9-4fe3-a8b0-569a93298701, a4b8f56f-7f1f-453e-8ddd-a8210fb4ec05

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
